{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>In the day</b>. The word יזועו is like ולא קם ולא זע ממנו (and none arose and none trembled from it)." "<b>מעטו</b>. A verb in pausal form, and the meaning is 'they ceased.' Some say the guards of the house are the ribs and the sides, and some say they are the four officials over each and every limb to guard it: the attractor, the digester, the retainer, and the purifier. Others interpret men of valor as the one who nourishes, the one who generates, the one who shapes, and the one near me — that the guards of the house are the hands together with the arms, which guard the body so that harm does not touch it, and the men of valor are the legs, and upon them it leans, and they totter, for they have no strength to stand; and the meaning of valor is strength, because the entire body rests upon them. And the millstones are the teeth, and those who look are the eyes."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The connection between the lemma 'ביום' and the discussion of יזועו is unclear; translated as found."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:18.475755806Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}